sweet fb: the panel wakes at the backlight service's level, not at 1 (0224).

all-20 (2026-11-18, sweetpanel=1 sweetfb_rate=60, AppleARMBacklight on by default): the first lock faded out normally;
after a wake the lock screen showed briefly and went black, or stayed dim, while the log had "display on" and
"brightness 128 FadePeriod 12124" and no later brightness 0. setPanelOn(true) ramps 1 -> fPanelLevel after its 120 ms
sleep-out wait; with the service, fPanelLevel is being moved by backboardd's 185 ms wake fade at that moment (or is still 1),
and the ramp's 16 steps (256 ms) end after the fade's last step, so the ramp's stale target stays on the panel.
With the service the sequence now sends the service's current level, read under the DSI lock. Without it: unchanged.
Not run on hardware yet.

diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
index ffdfcf5..f549061 100644
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
@@ -1296,7 +1296,26 @@ AppleCLCD::setPanelOn(bool on)
 	IOLockLock(fDsiLock);
 	done &= dsiSend(second, NULL, 0);
 	IOLockUnlock(fDsiLock);
-	if (on) {
+	if (on && fBacklightService) {
+		/*
+		 * 0224: AppleARMBacklight owns the level and backboardd starts its wake fade (0 -> 128 in
+		 * 185 ms) while this sequence is still in its 120 ms sleep-out wait. The ramp below read
+		 * fPanelLevel once, early in that fade or before it (all-20: 1), and its 16 steps ended
+		 * after the fade's last step: the panel stayed at level 1, black, with iOS at brightness
+		 * 128. Send the level the service holds instead, read under the DSI lock so that a step
+		 * of the fade either comes after this one or is the value read here.
+		 */
+		for (int i = 0; i < 2; i++) {
+			uint8_t hdr[4] = { 3, 0, 0x39, 0xc0 };
+			IOLockLock(fDsiLock);
+			uint32_t level = fPanelLevel;
+			uint8_t cmd[3] = { 0x51, (uint8_t)(level >> 8), (uint8_t)level };
+			done &= dsiSend(hdr, cmd, sizeof(cmd));
+			IOLockUnlock(fDsiLock);
+			IOLog("SWEET FB: panel on at the backlight service's level %#x\n", level);
+			IOSleep(20);
+		}
+	} else if (on) {
 		rampPanelLevel(1, fPanelLevel);
 	} else {
 		IOSleep(120);
